the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the age is *a number*.
    the risk category is *a text*.
    the is_affordable is *a truth value*.
    the status of the approval is *a text*.
    the rate of the approval is *a text*.

the templates are:
    the approval for *a number* and *a text* and *a truth value* is *a second text* with *a third text* under table approval.

the table approval is, with first match:
    age   | risk category | is_affordable | status     | rate
    >= 18 | "Medium"      | true          | "Approved" | "Best"
    >= 12 | "Medium"      | true          | "Approved" | "Standard"
    < 12  | "Low"         | true          | "Declined" | "Standard"

the knowledge base n0108_first_hitpolicy includes:

the text of the_model is at "sources/0108-first-hitpolicy.dmn".

rule approval_1 with provenance the model at decision Approval:
the status of the approval is a text if
    the age is a number
    and the risk category is a second text
    and the is_affordable is a truth value
    and the approval for the number and the second text and the truth value is the text with a third text under table approval
    otherwise the text is equal to "Declined".

rule approval_2 with provenance the model at decision Approval:
the rate of the approval is a text if
    the age is a number
    and the risk category is a second text
    and the is_affordable is a truth value
    and the approval for the number and the second text and the truth value is a third text with the text under table approval
    otherwise the text is equal to "Standard".

scenario t001 is, as stated in "0108-first-hitpolicy-test-01.xml" at test case 001:
    the age is 19.
    the risk category is "Medium".
    the is_affordable is true.
    q_d_status_of_the_approval expects answers ["the status of the approval is Approved"].
    q_d_rate_of_the_approval expects answers ["the rate of the approval is Best"].

scenario t002 is, as stated in "0108-first-hitpolicy-test-01.xml" at test case 002:
    the age is 13.
    the risk category is "Medium".
    the is_affordable is true.
    q_d_status_of_the_approval expects answers ["the status of the approval is Approved"].
    q_d_rate_of_the_approval expects answers ["the rate of the approval is Standard"].

scenario t003 is, as stated in "0108-first-hitpolicy-test-01.xml" at test case 003:
    the age is 10.
    the risk category is "Low".
    the is_affordable is true.
    q_d_status_of_the_approval expects answers ["the status of the approval is Declined"].
    q_d_rate_of_the_approval expects answers ["the rate of the approval is Standard"].

query q_d_rate_of_the_approval is:
    the rate of the approval is which text.

query q_d_status_of_the_approval is:
    the status of the approval is which text.

